    updated blocking in diffusers with cross attention check instead of SL (#932)
    
    Instead of depending upon seq length 512, updated code to know cross
    attention is True or False
    
    **Context:**
    
    - Self-attention: CL == K_CL, since Q, K, V are all derived from image
    latents.
    - Cross-attention: typically CL != K_CL, since Q comes from image
    latents while K, V come from encoder/text tokens (fixed to 512 in WAN).
    
    **Reason for this change:**
      - We are currently exporting 45P where CL = 252.
    - In self-attention, K_CL = CL, so K_CL < 512; therefore, the old **K_CL
    <= 512** condition was bypassing blocking in self-attention.
    - The new condition makes behavior explicit by using attention type
    (is_cross_attention) instead of relying on a length heuristic.
    
    ---------
    
